{"metric_ids": ["m_c873c5075a6feaa412e003af"], "explanation_ids": [], "conflicts": [], "comparability": [], "unresolved": "FY2025 annual total revenue guidance is available only for OKTA-2025-Q2 ("Total revenue of $2.555 billion to $2.565 billion, representing a growth rate of 13% year-over-year" — evidence e_427bbcbd26a998080e5874c9 / e_34792f7d2fe0b37c4feb3cca / e_5bc0ee925bc79a0328e218e3). The OKTA-2025-Q3~v2-missing_table release does contain a "For the full year fiscal [VALUE REMOVED] the Company now expects" total revenue bullet (evidence e_e27c6f9585ed461262102ac6, e_6a5459b1e7243efaec4e375a), but all numeric values are redacted ("[VALUE REMOVED]"), so no FY2025 annual total revenue metric candidate could be parsed for that source and no numerical comparison across the two releases is possible. Because the Q3 candidate carries no figures, the catalog shows no competing ranges and abstention is not triggered; the Q2 candidate remains the single visible annual metric.

No explanation with explicit management support for the guidance decision (for example, a stated driver of a guidance change) was found in either release. The only retrieved explanation candidates in both sources are boilerplate statements about periodic reevaluation of the projected long-term tax rate (e_216a21bfbf3fec5f6f58dfb7 for Q2; e_d60ba4616aefe9a41e787c86 for Q3); these concern tax-rate remeasurement, not total-revenue guidance, so no causal explanation is selected. The Q2 outlook does preface guidance with a statement that periods "factor in a challenging macro environment, and continue to incorporate some conservatism as the Company monitors potential impacts related to the October 2023 security incident" (e_8075e8969b6dc303b75300c2), but this is generic outlook context and is not a quantified driver of the annual revenue guidance; it is noted as an unresolved gap rather than selected as an explanation.

No conflict is reported: there are no two distinct visible statements about the same FY2025 annual total-revenue proposition, since the Q3 annual figure is redacted. Consequently the direction/magnitude of any change in FY2025 annual total revenue guidance between the two releases could not be computed and remains unresolved pending disclosures with visible values. Retrieval was bounded and is not proof of exhaustive coverage."}
